      "title": "Temporary Production Cook",
      "description": "Temporary Production Cook - Marquette, Michigan, United States Temporary Production Cook - Marquette, Michigan, United States Skip to Main Content Northern Michigan University Careers Kiosk mode Temporary Production Cook 495130 Marquette, Michigan, 49855 Dining Services-Central Office Temporary Closing on: Nov 2 2026 Position Title: Temporary Production Cook Department: Dining Services-Central Office Term of Assignment: Term FLSA Status: Non-Exempt = overtime eligible Work Schedule: Variable days/hours/locations; between the hours of 5:30 am and 11:00 pm, as determined by the needs of the operation. Salary: Hourly rate: $18.59 Travel: No travel Brief Statement of Duties Brief Statement of Duties: This is a posting for part-time temporary positions which are used to supplement and augment the regular NMU workforce. This position is primarily responsible for food preparation and cooking. The length of hire might vary from 1 day to 4 months. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: High School Graduation or Equivalent Required Specialized Training/Certifications: Food Service Sanitation Certification (ServSafe) or the ability to obtain within six months from the start of employment. Required Minimum Work Experience: Eighteen months of food service experience in kitchen production while working in a quantity food service setting (e.g. Fast Casual, Quick Service Restaurant experience, large production retail chain/branded setting). Knowledge, Skills, Abilities, or Attributes Required for Satisfactory Performance of the Position Duties: Customer and Personal Service-Knowledge of principles and processes for providing customer and personal services. This includes customer needs assessment, meeting quality standards for services, and evaluation of customer satisfaction. Active Listening-Giving full attention to what other people are saying; taking time to understand the points being made; asking questions as appropriate; and not interrupting at inappropriate times. Instructing-Teaching others how to do something. Speaking-Talking to others to convey information effectively. Service Orientation-Actively looking for ways to help people. Social Perceptiveness-Being aware of others' reactions and understanding why they react as they do. Possess the physical capability to perform all of the duties and responsibilities of the position. Oral Comprehension-The ability to listen to and understand information and ideas presented through spoken words and sentences. Manual Dexterity-The ability to quickly move your hand, your hand together with your arm, or your two hands to grasp, manipulate, or assemble objects. Problem Sensitivity-The ability to tell when something is wrong or is likely to go wrong. It does not involve solving the problem, only recognizing there is a problem. Additional Desirable Qualifications Additional Desirable Qualifications: Food Service Sanitation Certification. Leadership ability demonstrated by experience. Willingness to improve skill level. Experience in gourmet/banquet/catering cooking/preparation. Vocational education training in baking, cooking, salad making, etc. Special Instructions to Applicants: Submit application, cover letter, resume and references. This position is not currently available for sponsorship. Contact Information: Brenda Bickler, Employment Specialist, 906-227-2114 NMU is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now! Recently Posted Jobs Economics/Assistant Professor/Three Year Term Economics Teach courses in Money and Banking, Intermediate Macroeconomics, Principles of Macroeconomics, and be prepared to teach Introduction to Economics and Principles of Microeconomics. The normal teaching load is three courses (12 credit hours) per semester, with up to three different course preparations per semester. Additional responsibilities include service at the department, college, and university levels, and student advising. Resources are available for engaging in professional development, research, and conference travel. Desirable qualifications: Being able to teach Comparative Economic Systems and American Economic History. Being able to integrate emerging technologies, including AI, into teaching and other professional activities in innovative and effective ways. This position is campus-based and is not currently eligible for sponsorship. Earth, Environmental, and Geographical Sciences/Assistant Professor in Environmental Hazards/Tenure Track Earth, Env, & Geog Sciences The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses that complement and strengthen the Department’s curriculum, maintain an active and student-engaged research program in environmental hazards and applied GIS or a closely related field, publish in peer-reviewed outlets, and pursue external funding opportunities. Additional responsibilities include advising undergraduate and graduate students and contributing to departmental, university, and professional service. This position is not available for sponsorship. This is a campus-based position. Manager-Grant Accounting/Accounting Services Controllers Office Plan, develop and refine operating procedures and computerized systems for financial reporting. Monitor, review and document University financial transactions for compliance with accounting principles, University policies, federal circulars and Internal Revenue Service rules and regulations. Prepare and/or assist with preparation of many of the University's financial statements, annual audits, income tax return, revenue projections of University endowments and expenditure projections for special projects. Responsible for all post award financial management functions, including expenditure monitoring, financial reporting, grant close-out, and audit. Biology - Forensics/Assistant Professor/Tenure Track Biology The Tenure Track Assistant Professor position requires a Ph.D. in forensic biology or a related field. Ph.D must be earned by August 15, 2027. The assignments will include teaching a range of courses related to forensic science such as Introduction to Forensic Science, Forensic Biology, Forensic Microscopy, Forensic Entomology, other areas of forensic science, a career seminar, or advanced courses in areas of specialty. Assignments may also include teaching in related fields including human anatomy & physiology. The selected candidate will be expected to develop a research program in forensic biology incorporating undergraduate and graduate students. Preference will be given to those applicants whose work engages decomposition ecology or related specialties in entomology, microbiology, morphological decomposition, and postmortem interval estimation. This is a campus based position. This position is not currently available for sponsorship. Temporary Production Cook Dining Services-Central Office This is a posting for part-time temporary positions which are used to supplement and augment the regular NMU workforce. This position is primarily responsible for food preparation and cooking. The length of hire might vary from 1 day to 4 months. Philosophy/Assistant Professor/Three Year Term Philosophy Brief Statement of Duties: The course load will be 12 credits per semester, with multiple preps each term. The teaching responsibilities will include various applied ethics courses (computer, legal, medical) as well as a course in social and political philosophy. There will also be additional service responsibilities in support of the department, college, and university. The appointment will require having an active research agenda. This is a campus-based position. This position is currently not available for sponsorship. Sign up for job alerts By signing up for job alerts, you will be notified of vacancies based on your career category selection. You are able to sign up for as many career categories as you would like. Job Alert 1d095189 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select mu